      "elapsed_ms": 17846.70029199333,
      "final_message": "`service2.compute_fee(1000, \"gold\")` returns 480. Running it directly gives the same result.\n\n`service2.py` only uses two modules, `pricing` and `discounts`:\n1. **Base fee:** `pricing.base_fee(1000)` = 500 + 1000 // 10 = 600.\n2. **Discount:** `discounts.apply_discount(600, \"gold\")` takes off the gold tier's 20%: 600 \u2212 (600 \u00d7 20) // 100 = 480.\n\nNothing calls `decoy_tax.py` or `decoy_shipping.py`, so they don't change the result.\n\nANSWER: 480",
      "final_message_source": "stdout_response",
